1.1.text:
CHAPTER III
RESPONSIBILITIES
Article 4
(1) The Regional Government is responsible for implementing prevention efforts against the occurrence of violence in the form of:
a. Collecting data and information about women and children victims of violence in accordance with Laws and Regulations;
b. Conducting education on anti-violence values towards women and children;
c. Conducting socialization of Laws and Regulations related to the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence;
d. Conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of services and protection for women and children victims of violence;
(2) To anticipate the occurrence of acts of violence, the Regional Government provides and organizes services for victims in the form of:
a. Establishing and facilitating the operation of integrated service institutions for victims by involving community elements;
b. Encouraging community awareness of the importance of protection for victims.
(3) The Regional Government in providing and organizing services as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands or other persons who are legally responsible for the victim.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
The Principles of Service and Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence are:
a. Respect and recognition of equal human rights and dignity;
b. Respect for the rights of victims;
c. Justice and gender equality;
d. Non-discriminatory; and
e. Best interests of victims.

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF WEST MANGGARAI,

Considering:
that violence and discrimination in any form against women and children constitutes a violation of Human Rights; therefore, violence and discrimination against women and children occurring in West Manggarai Regency must receive optimal services and protection;
that the provision of services for women victims of violence and child protection is one of the authorities of the regency government in accordance with the provisions of Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government; therefore, it needs to be regulated by a Regional Regulation;
that based on the considerations as referred to above, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Services and Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of:
1.
2.
3.

Article 8
(1) The forms of services and protection for victims organized by P3A consist of:
 a. Medical services in the form of treatment and recovery of physical injuries aimed at restoring the physical condition of victims carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
 b. Medicolegal services constitute a form of medical service for evidentiary purposes in the legal field;
 c. Psychosocial services constitute services provided by companions in order to restore the traumatic condition of victims, including the provision of safe houses to protect victims from various threats and intimidation for victims and to provide social support so that victims have self-confidence, strength and independence in resolving their problems;
 d. Legal services to assist victims in undergoing the judicial process;
 e. Economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and providing economic access so that victims can be independent.
(2) Further provisions regarding the mechanism of services and protection as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be organized according to Standard Operational Procedure (SOP) which will be further regulated by Regent Regulation.

